# The transpiler rewrite's strict xfail list (TESTING.md, "Golden gate").
#
#   <input-set>/<relpath> <target> <reason>
#
# <target> is a dialect name, or `parse` (the output file's stem under the
# input's golden directory). The `ir` and `report` lines went with the IR
# (phase 6): `golden diff` passes over a baseline's `ir.json` and
# `report.json`. `golden diff --xfail` fails on
# any difference not listed here, and on a listed line that is now identical
# (XPASS): delete the line then. Every line is a reviewed, intended change.
#
# Baseline: baseline-ccc7930-fx18 (TESTING.md "Golden gate"), recorded from
# batch-11b ccc7930 (p7-integrate 94743c7) by team-lead's batch-11b gate (D47;
# batches 8 to 11b landed on fx17). Every line this list held against
# baseline-1298f0b-fx17 was a reviewed, intended change and is now the
# baseline; the list starts empty. A new line goes under a section header
# naming its ledger row.

# S2: P5-001-s3: a `.step` (Xyce, LTspice, a Spectre `sweep`, an HSPICE `.temp` list) over the temperature,
# a parameter of the deck's top or a top-level R, C, L, V, I runs on ngspice as `foreach` loops of the `.control`
# script (`alterparam` + `reset`, `option temp=`, `alter`), the first `.step` innermost; it was refused W0016.
